{
  "schema_version": "component_profile.v1",
  "component_id": "cvw",
  "kind": "cpu",
  "description": "CORE-V Wally (CVW) at the pinned upstream revision, declared at its AHB-Lite external bus. The CPU is the AHB manager: it drives HADDR/HWDATA/HWSTRB/HTRANS/HSIZE/HBURST/HPROT/HWRITE/HMASTLOCK and receives the subordinate's completion on HREADYEXT/HRDATAEXT/HRESPEXT. Read data is HRDATAEXT and not HRDATA because src/ebu/ebu.sv deliberately has no HRDATA port (\"HRDATA is sent to all controllers at the core level\"). HADDR is 34 bits while the data path is 32, so the address width is deliberately not the data width. The boundary is elaborated through the repository-authored typed top configs/cpus/cvw/cvw_ahb_cpu_top.sv, required because wallypipelinedsoc takes #(parameter cvw_t P) - a struct-typed localparam that cannot be overridden from the Verilator command line - and because CVW's own testbench/wallywrapper.sv declares these signals as internal wires instead of ports. Every port, width and direction below was produced by myfuzz.composition.source_elaboration.extract_physical_ports over the Verilator JSON run recorded in configs/soc/closures/cvw.json; none was written by hand. No harness has been generated or bound for this boundary and no real AHB-Lite transaction has been run.",
